{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tremolo ornament can be used to indicate single-note, double-note, or unmeasured tremolos. Single-note"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tremolos use the single type, double-note tremolos use the start and stop types, and unmeasured tremolos use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the unmeasured type. The default is “single” for compatibility with Version 1.1. The text of the element"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indicates the number of tremolo marks and is an integer from 0 to 8. Note that the number of attached beams is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not included in this value, but is represented separately using the beam element. The value should be 0 for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unmeasured tremolos."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTremolo"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When using double-note tremolos, the duration of each note in the tremolo should correspond to half of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"notated type value. A time-modification element should also be added with an actual-notes value of 2 and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"normal-notes value of 1. If used within a tuplet, this 2\/1 ratio should be multiplied by the existing tuplet","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ratio.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The smufl attribute specifies the glyph to use from the SMuFL Tremolos range for an unmeasured tremolo. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ignored for other tremolo types. The SMuFL buzzRoll glyph is used by default if the attribute is missing.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Using repeater beams for indicating tremolos is deprecated as of MusicXML 3.0.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<tremolo>"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo\/init(value:kind:position:font:color:placement:smufl:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo\/color","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo\/font","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo\/kind-swift.property","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo\/placement","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo\/position","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo\/smufl","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo\/value"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo\/Kind-swift.enum"],"anchor":"Enumerations","title":"Enumerations"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo\/Equatable-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"va